  "lines": [
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Cars are supposed to stay on the road, but Tesla just made one leave it.",
      "emphasis": "leave it",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "road"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "And that one viral clip is mixing different machines and different tricks.",
      "emphasis": "different tricks",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "rocket"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "In the next few minutes, we'll go through how it drives, how it sticks to a wall upside down,",
      "emphasis": "upside down",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "wheel",
        "fan"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "how the rocket version gets into the air, and whether any of this is a real car or just a show.",
      "emphasis": "real car",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "stage"
      ],
      "label": "REAL OR SHOW?",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Let's start with the boring part, because that's where the whole thing begins.",
      "emphasis": "boring part",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "battery"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "The battery stores the energy, and the power electronics decide how much goes to the motors.",
      "emphasis": "motors",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "battery",
        "chip",
        "motor"
      ],
      "label": "BATTERY TO MOTOR",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "The motors turn the wheels, and the tires push against the road.",
      "emphasis": "push",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "wheel",
        "road"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "There's no petrol and no rocket in this part, it's a normal electric car doing what electric cars do.",
      "emphasis": "normal electric car",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "electric car"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "Every crazy moment in that video starts with plain driving.",
      "emphasis": "plain driving",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "road"
      ],
      "label": "PLAIN DRIVING",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "How does a car hold on when it's upside down?",
      "emphasis": "upside down",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "curved wall"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That's the fans.",
      "emphasis": "fans",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "fan"
      ],
      "label": "FANS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "They suck the air out from under the car, and a seal around the bottom stops new air rushing back in.",
      "emphasis": "seal",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "fan",
        "arrow",
        "seal"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "The pressure under the car drops, and the normal air above pushes the whole car down onto the surface.",
      "emphasis": "pushes",
      "visual": "spike_vs_curve",
      "subjects": [
        "arrow",
        "sports car"
      ],
      "label": "LOW PRESSURE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That presses the tires harder into the surface, so they grip more and the car can take corners faster.",
      "emphasis": "grip more",
      "visual": "gauge",
      "subjects": [
        "tire"
      ],
      "label": "GRIP",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "That's how Tesla drove it up a curved wall and held it upside down with the fans running.",
      "emphasis": "curved wall",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "curved wall"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "But understand this, the fans don't lift anything, they glue the car down.",
      "emphasis": "glue the car down",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "fan",
        "arrow up"
      ],
      "label": "NO LIFT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "Anyone calling that part flying is wrong, that's grip.",
      "emphasis": "that's grip",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "tire",
        "road"
      ],
      "label": "GRIP, NOT FLIGHT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "The part where it really goes into the air is a different car.",
      "emphasis": "different car",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "rocket car"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Tesla lists three versions, Performance, Thrust and Rocket, and each one has different hardware.",
      "emphasis": "three versions",
      "visual": "icon_grid",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "fan",
        "rocket"
      ],
      "label": "3 VERSIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "The Performance one keeps two seats and the fans.",
      "emphasis": "two seats",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "seat",
        "fan"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "The Rocket one has one seat and extra thrusters for lift and rotation.",
      "emphasis": "one seat",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "seat",
        "thruster"
      ],
      "label": "ROCKET",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "Inside it, high pressure tanks feed what's called cold gas thrusters.",
      "emphasis": "cold gas thrusters",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "gas tank",
        "nozzle"
      ],
      "label": "COLD GAS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "The gas shoots out of nozzles around the car one way, and the car gets pushed the other way.",
      "emphasis": "pushed",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "nozzle",
        "arrow"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That's Newton's third law, the same cold gas idea NASA uses for short moves in space.",
      "emphasis": "Newton's third law",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "satellite",
        "arrow"
      ],
      "label": "NEWTON'S 3RD LAW",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "But the tanks only hold so much gas, so the push only lasts a moment.",
      "emphasis": "a moment",
      "visual": "clock",
      "subjects": [
        "gas tank",
        "clock"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "That moment is enough to lift it, flip it or roll it, and bring it back down on its wheels.",
      "emphasis": "flip it",
      "visual": "staircase",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "arrow"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "That one really does leave the ground, but it's a one seat prototype, not the car you'd drive to work.",
      "emphasis": "prototype",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "rocket car"
      ],
      "label": "PROTOTYPE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Now, is this a real flying car or a show?",
      "emphasis": "show",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "stage"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Tesla itself lists the Rocket model as not approved for public roads.",
      "emphasis": "not approved",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "road sign"
      ],
      "label": "NOT ROAD LEGAL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Independent reporting called the car at the event a one off demonstration.",
      "emphasis": "one off",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "camera",
        "sports car"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "And we've seen one good jump, nothing yet like repeated launches and landings that prove the fans, seals and tanks hold up.",
      "emphasis": "one good jump",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "fan",
        "seal",
        "gas tank"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Then there's everything a real car has to survive, a crash, a hard landing, noise, servicing and the extra weight.",
      "emphasis": "crash",
      "visual": "icon_grid",
      "subjects": [
        "crash",
        "wrench",
        "weight"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "So the driving is real, the grip is real, and the flying is a prototype.",
      "emphasis": "flying is a prototype",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "wheel",
        "fan",
        "rocket"
      ],
      "label": "VERDICT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "Until Tesla shows repeat flights and gets it certified for safety, that's all it is.",
      "emphasis": "certified",
      "visual": "gauge",
      "subjects": [
        "shield"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The simple version is, motors move the car, fans keep it stuck down, and gas thrusters push one special version into the air for a moment.",
      "emphasis": "for a moment",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "motor",
        "fan",
        "thruster"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The car left the road, but whether it ever becomes a flying car you can own is still decided on the ground.",
      "emphasis": "on the ground",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "sports car",
        "road"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "cta",
      "text": "And if you want the next big tech clip broken down like this, follow the channel.",
      "emphasis": "follow the channel",
      "visual": "logo_end",
      "subjects": [
        "logo"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": true
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "cta",
      "text": "So here's the question, should Tesla certify the Rocket Roadster, or keep it as a prototype?",
      "emphasis": "certify",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "shield",
        "rocket car"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    }
  ]
}